# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[specific]] [[system]] of [[electrical]] [[circuit]]s in a particular [[device]]; {{lb|en|uncountable}} the [[design#Noun|design]] of such a system.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ernst H[enry] Krause|authorlink=Ernst Henry Krause|title=High Altitude Research with V-2 Rockets|editor=[[w:Luther P. Eisenhart|Luther P[fahler] Eisenhart]]|journal={{w|Proceedings of the American Philosophical Society}}|location=Philadelphia, Pa.|publisher={{w|American Philosophical Society}}{{nb...|Independence Square, Philadelphia 6}}|date=25 April 1947|volume=91|issue=5|section=figure 3 caption|page=432|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=zjPVAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA432|column=2|issn=0003-049X|oclc=299393900|passage=Telemetering transmitter removed from its pressurized container. The '''circuitry''' for each of the 23 channels can be quickly unplugged for servicing.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Lew Allen, Jr.|authorlink=Lew Allen|author2=James L. Beavers, II|author3=William A. Whitaker|author4=Jasper A. Welch, Jr.|author5=Roddy B. Walton|title=Project Jason Measurement of Trapped Electrons from a Nuclear Device by Sounding Rockets|journal={{w|Journal of Geophysical Research}}|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher={{w|American Geophysical Union}}|month=August|year=1959|volume=64|issue=8|page=894|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=W0cPAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA894|column=1|issn=0148-0227|oclc=1039445258|passage=After jettison of nose cap, all the detector '''circuitry''' became exposed to the radiation environment.}}
#* {{quote-us-patent|en|author=Wallace Keith Larkin|title=Acoustical Communications Headset|number=3,993,879|date=24 March 1975|column=1|columnurl=https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/e3/09/34/c5b2583829ac3d/US3993879.pdf#page=4|passage=Prior art radio and telephone communication headsets typically incorporate a microphone and receiver which require amplifier or other appropriate electronic impedance matching circuits for interface with the console, or at least electrically conductive wires to similar electronic '''circuitry''' located in the console.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=A. A. Dowd|title={{w|Steven Spielberg}} Finds Fun, and maybe even a Soul, in the Pandering Pastiche of ''[[w:Ready Player One (film)|Ready Player One]]''|url=https://film.avclub.com/steven-spielberg-finds-fun-and-maybe-even-a-soul-in-the-1824094654|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180531213806/https://film.avclub.com/steven-spielberg-finds-fun-and-maybe-even-a-soul-in-the-1824094654|archivedate=31 May 2018|work={{w|The A.V. Club}}|date=26 March 2018|passage=Before he died, James Halliday ({{w|Mark Rylance}}), the hermit-like, socially maladjusted tech genius who created The Oasis, hid an Easter egg somewhere in the '''circuitry''', scattering bread crumbs that lead to its location. Find the egg, and the mogul’s fortune—along with total control of his digital fiefdom—is yours. It’s the ultimate capitalist scavenger hunt!}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Electrical circuits considered as a [[group#Noun|group]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=William Jury|title=Green River Greets the Space Age: Work Begins on New $16,000,000 Research Center|editor=Chester Chatfield|magazine=The Boeing Magazine|location=Seattle, Wash.|publisher=Public Relations Office, [[w:Boeing|The Boeing Company]]|month=February|year=1964|volume=XXXIV|issue=2|page=11|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ctYMAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA73-IA43|column=3|oclc=1052694660|passage=In the microelectronics area, research and development efforts will concentrate on thin film '''circuitry''', packaging and solid state electronics (work with transistors and the like). [...] The savings in weight over old-fashioned '''circuitry''' are important when the cost of items in orbit is figured at $1,000 per pound.}}
